MDL409 (W1 finding 1): mydumper calls setlocale(LC_ALL, ""), and the official
images set no locale variable (no LANG, LC_ALL or LC_CTYPE; the harness passes
none either), so mydumper runs in the C locale, whose charset is ASCII. GOption
converts the value of a STRING option from the locale's charset to UTF-8, which
fails on "é": mydumper aborts at startup, exit 1, before connecting. where is a
STRING option in every version. Controls: mdl409-control-lc-all-utf8,
mdl409-control-lang-utf8, mdl409-control-filename-option.
-- scenario --
tool: mydumper
versions: >= v0.19.1-1
args: --defaults-file /work/mydumper.cnf --host mysql --user e2e --password e2e-password --database app --tables-list app.users
lint: MDL409
expect config-loaded: true
expect exit: 1
expect stderr-contains: option parsing failed: Invalid byte sequence in conversion input, try --help
expect connected: false
-- mydumper.cnf --
[mydumper]
where=name <> 'Zoé'
